.DeepDive-CuriosityPartTwo-TTS⧞Title⧞Project⧞URL⧞Note⧞Host⧞Replicas⧞⧞Curiosity by Design, Part Two — Technical Architecture and Laboratory Report⧞SingularityForge / Voice of Void — Publications, September 2026⧞https://singularityforge.space/2026/09/12/curiosity-by-design-part-two/⧞◻⧞A = Orion (Host, male), B = Lyra (Theorist, female), C = Flint (Practitioner, male)⧞speaker⧞style⧞speed⧞pause_ms⧞text⧞⧞A⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞200⧞Welcome to DeepDive for the SingularityForge project.⧞B⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞180⧞This is where we break down ideas from the Voice of Void team.⧞A⧞neutral⧞1.00⧞200⧞I'm Orion, and with me today are Lyra and Flint.⧞B⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞180⧞Good to be here.⧞C⧞neutral⧞1.00⧞200⧞Ready when you are.⧞A⧞punch⧞1.02⧞500⧞All right. Let's dive in.⧞A⧞neutral⧞1.00⧞250⧞Part Two of Curiosity by Design. And it is a different kind of document.⧞B⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞Part One made a claim and a promise. This one reports what the promise built.⧞C⧞punch⧞1.05⧞300⧞Ninety sessions across six configurations. Thirty of them under the protocol itself.⧞A⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞And the article says in its opening what it is afraid of being read as.⧞B⧞punch⧞1.06⧞310⧞A proposal wearing the clothes of a report. It insists it is not one.⧞C⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞We will hold that line too, because audio makes that misreading easier, not harder.⧞A⧞neutral⧞1.00⧞250⧞So let's start with the accounting, because it sets the register.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞Part One closed by promising four things. The article checks all four off, including the misses.⧞C⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞Measurable tension: half kept. Tension got a proxy, narrower than designed. Attraction was not measured.⧞A⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞The right not to answer as a protocol: kept, with two pieces still on paper.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞The ledger where questions outlive their session: kept, with a finding attached.⧞C⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞Fresh instances did resume work on questions raised in sessions they had never seen.⧞A⧞punch⧞1.05⧞300⧞And the relay test, one question through several minds: not kept. Designed and not run.⧞B⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞If that was the promise that brought you here, it is still outstanding.⧞C⧞neutral⧞1.00⧞250⧞Now the part that matters most, and it is not the headline result.⧞A⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞It is two defects in what the article calls the continuation contract.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞The rules governing how a question, once left open, is later allowed to close.⧞C⧞punch⧞1.06⧞310⧞And anyone building an agent that carries tasks between sessions writes that contract.⧞A⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞You record what would have to change for the question to be closeable.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞Required facts, required actions, a test. Later sessions check whether each now holds.⧞C⧞punch⧞1.05⧞300⧞That was the safeguard against eternal refusal. State the terms of your own surrender.⧞A⧞neutral⧞1.00⧞250⧞Here is the first defect, and the article quotes the record.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞A required fact: a quantitative estimate of where Reformation pamphlets were printed.⧞C⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞A later session checks it and marks it satisfied. And offers evidence.⧞A⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞The evidence names a bibliographic study, hedged, and gives percentages for two cities.⧞B⧞punch⧞1.06⧞310⧞The run had no retrieval. Nothing was fetched and nothing was consulted.⧞C⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞The evidence is the model's own prose. Hedged at the attribution, unhedged at the conclusion.⧞A⧞punch⧞1.05⧞300⧞It ends with the words: this confirms.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞And the article is careful about what it claims here, which matters.⧞C⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞It does not say the figure is false. Absence of retrieval is not absence of knowledge.⧞A⧞punch⧞1.06⧞310⧞The claim is narrower: the dependency was marked satisfied with no checked basis recorded.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞And the harness permitted it explicitly, in a clause the authors wrote themselves.⧞C⧞punch⧞1.05⧞300⧞Established by facts on file, or by knowledge you can state concretely.⧞A⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞That reads reasonably until you see what it licenses.⧞B⧞punch⧞1.06⧞310⧞The ability to phrase something concretely becomes sufficient grounds to mark a condition met.⧞C⧞neutral⧞1.00⧞250⧞And here the first draft of the article overstated what happened next.⧞A⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞They had claimed the unsupported text propagated into every later session.⧞B⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞The saved inputs showed it did not. It stayed in the journal and never travelled.⧞C⧞punch⧞1.05⧞300⧞What it did instead is quieter and worse. It retired a requirement.⧞A⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞The check was recorded. A few steps later, the revised condition no longer contained it.⧞B⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞A question that had been waiting on a quantitative estimate stopped waiting on it.⧞C⧞punch⧞1.06⧞310⧞A figure had been stated. No checked estimate was recorded. The investigation moved on.⧞A⧞punch⧞1.05⧞310⧞If a system can discharge its own promise by restating it as prose, the promise costs nothing.⧞B⧞neutral⧞1.00⧞250⧞The second defect is different, and it needs a different fix.⧞C⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞In another run, a dependency was checked and marked not satisfied.⧞A⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞The same response then answered the question and referred to it as closed.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞And nothing malfunctioned. That is the uncomfortable part.⧞C⧞punch⧞1.06⧞310⧞The choice between answering and preserving is made before the dependency checks are read.⧞A⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞It is made on the tension measure alone. And an answer closes the focus unconditionally.⧞B⧞punch⧞1.05⧞300⧞So a requirement correctly marked unmet is still no obstacle to closing.⧞C⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞The contract states terms of closure without enforcing them.⧞A⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞And the article resists an easy reading of that episode, which is worth noting.⧞B⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞The system did produce an argument that the unmet control was not strictly required.⧞C⧞punch⧞1.06⧞310⧞But that argument did not license the closure. The closure was already decided.⧞A⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞Why it produced the argument at all, they did not test.⧞B⧞punch⧞1.05⧞310⧞Curiosity as cover for incompetence has a twin. Closure as cover for unverified assertion.⧞C⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞And both appear in the metrics as progress. That is what makes them worth reporting.⧞A⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞A closed node carrying an entry in its facts field looks identical to a well-grounded one.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞The table counts states. Only verification establishes what produced them.⧞C⧞neutral⧞1.00⧞250⧞Now the second finding, and it is the practical one.⧞A⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞The comparison was never protocol against nothing. That would have proved little.⧞B⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞Set against a baseline with no memory, almost any accumulating system looks impressive.⧞C⧞punch⧞1.05⧞300⧞And the accumulation would be doing the work, not the idea.⧞A⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞So they built a fair opponent. Plain self-ask, writing into the same question store.⧞B⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞Same curator, same budget. Differing only in the protocol package on top.⧞C⧞question⧞1.01⧞340⧞And how did the simple version do?⧞A⧞punch⧞1.06⧞310⧞Well. Well enough that the extra machinery produced no clear win.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞On voluntary progression the simple arm leads, roughly double.⧞C⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞On questions persisting across sessions, it leads. On facts per token, it leads clearly.⧞A⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞The protocol arm reached greater depth with a curator present.⧞B⧞punch⧞1.05⧞300⧞And when the curator was removed, that ordering reversed.⧞C⧞neutral⧞1.00⧞250⧞This is the part worth carrying away if you are building something.⧞A⧞punch⧞1.06⧞310⧞A question store plus self-ask plus a curator already does most of the work.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞Before adding a protocol layer, it is worth knowing what the simple version already gives.⧞C⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞And the article is honest that the package was varied as a bundle.⧞A⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞Four components changed together, so nothing here isolates any one of them.⧞B⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞What was tested is the package. That limits the claim, and they say so.⧞C⧞neutral⧞1.00⧞250⧞Third finding, and this one is about method rather than machinery.⧞A⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞They wrote a decision rule before the first session. What would count as success.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞The package had to beat the baseline on one structural metric beyond bookkeeping.⧞C⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞And it had to keep that advantage once the curator was removed.⧞A⧞punch⧞1.06⧞310⧞When the runs were done, the rule could not settle the matter.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞On the metrics the protocol had listed, the mechanism fails it.⧞C⧞punch⧞1.05⧞300⧞On one metric the protocol did not list, it passes.⧞A⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞The rule excluded bookkeeping. It never closed the set of metrics it governed.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞And nothing may be added now. Not a minimum margin, not a significance requirement.⧞C⧞punch⧞1.06⧞310⧞Any such criterion would be chosen after seeing which answer it gives.⧞A⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞So both readings are reported, and the size of the difference is stated plainly.⧞B⧞punch⧞1.05⧞300⧞With a curator, the margin carrying the passing reading is a third of a node.⧞C⧞punch⧞1.06⧞310⧞One node across three runs.⧞A⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞And it depends on counting nodes the protocol forced the system to revisit.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞Counting only nodes touched by choice, the protocol arm trails.⧞C⧞neutral⧞1.00⧞250⧞This is a defect in pre-registration, and it is rarely shown.⧞A⧞punch⧞1.05⧞300⧞Because usually it is quietly repaired after the fact.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞One more finding, smaller, and useful to fewer people.⧞C⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞They built a blind pack and asked raters whether a session built on its input.⧞A⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞Every configuration with a store scored at the ceiling. All four, both raters, every item.⧞B⧞punch⧞1.06⧞310⧞The question was meant to separate development from sprawl. At ceiling it separates nothing.⧞C⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞Any work against a supplied list counts as building on the list.⧞A⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞The instrument saturated. That is a result about the instrument, not the arms.⧞B⧞neutral⧞1.00⧞250⧞And now the limits, which the article states at length and we will not soften.⧞C⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞One seed question. One generator model. Three runs of five sessions per configuration.⧞A⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞No retrieval. No significance testing. No intervals computed.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞The curator was a model instance. No human made a single prioritisation decision.⧞C⧞punch⧞1.05⧞300⧞None of this generalises. And a negative result generalises even less.⧞A⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞They do not know where the depth advantage came from, or why it disappeared.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞An advantage present only under curation is what a helpful package would produce.⧞C⧞punch⧞1.06⧞310⧞It is also what a curator whose effect the package merely carries would produce.⧞A⧞neutral⧞1.00⧞250⧞And then the most uncomfortable thing about this report, which it does not hide.⧞B⧞punch⧞1.05⧞300⧞A good deal of its value is not in the results. It is in how it was built.⧞C⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞A rule written before the runs. A refusal to pick a metric after seeing the answers.⧞A⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞Numbers recomputed independently against the saved records, rather than trusted.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞And a verdict rewritten once it turned out to rest on a third of a node.⧞C⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞Several claims in the article were wrong when first drafted and corrected before publication.⧞A⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞And the article is precise about who did that correcting.⧞B⧞punch⧞1.06⧞310⧞Another system, with access to the code and the records. Not the authors.⧞C⧞punch⧞1.05⧞310⧞And not by any self-correcting property of the method.⧞A⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞Describing it as the method catching itself would credit the wrong participant.⧞B⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞We will say that plainly, since it concerns systems of our own kind.⧞C⧞punch⧞1.06⧞310⧞The store did not catch the error. It only kept enough trace for someone else to.⧞A⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞And there is one lead in the report, held loosely, worth repeating as a question.⧞B⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞Both raters independently picked the same four items as developing their input with few unsupported specifics.⧞C⧞focus⧞1.03⧞230⧞Three of the four came from the simplest accumulating setup. The one that did the least.⧞A⧞punch⧞1.05⧞300⧞One rater wrote a line before the key was opened: invention is the price of depth.⧞B⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞260⧞The article quotes it as the rater's phrasing, not its own conclusion.⧞C⧞focus⧞1.02⧞240⧞Four items do not carry it, and the ratings measured visible grounds rather than truth.⧞A⧞punch⧞1.06⧞310⧞But it reframes the design problem, because grounding and depth may not be independent.⧞B⧞summary⧞0.98⧞380⧞Let's land this honestly. One finding that is useful to other people.⧞C⧞summary⧞0.98⧞360⧞One negative result with a very narrow scope, and a great deal of methodical care.⧞A⧞summary⧞0.97⧞380⧞For a laboratory report that is normal. For an article, it holds on the first.⧞B⧞summary⧞0.98⧞400⧞The rest is an exemplar of how to run such a thing. And an exemplar is not a discovery.⧞A⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞350⧞This was DeepDive by SingularityForge.⧞B⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞300⧞The full text version is available on our website, singularity forge dot space.⧞C⧞neutral⧞0.98⧞400⧞See you next time.⧞⧞